+# Pantry search
+
+For whoever changes pantry search or enables its cache. Search can reuse recent results from Redis to reduce repeated
+item queries during slow Saturday mornings. The requested cache is optional so the app can still run on Postgres alone.
+
+## Results and freshness
+
+[The catalog query](../../larder/catalog.py) keeps the existing Postgres full-text matching and name ordering. With
+caching enabled, identical search strings share results, including empty results, for 15 seconds. Stock and item
+edits can take that long to appear; cached stock is display information, not a reservation or a checkout guarantee.
+There is no write-side invalidation in this repository. Disable the cache when immediate freshness is required.
+
+Redis failures, an unavailable Python client and malformed entries fall back to Postgres. Cache connections and
+reads have short timeouts and no automatic retries. Database errors still propagate. Cache failures are logged
+without the connection URL.
+
+## Configuration
+
+Install the Python dependency with `python3 -m pip install -r requirements.txt`. Set `LARDER_REDIS_URL` in the web
+app environment, for example `redis://localhost:6379/0`, and restart the app to enable caching. Leave it unset and
+restart to disable it. Use a separate Redis database for each deployment or pantry database: keys are shared across
+web processes and assume the repository's single pantry database. Redis must be private to trusted app processes.
+
+## Known limits
+
+The request names Tom to run Redis. This is an explicit exception to the existing
+[service operating rule](../philosophy.md#tenets): the repository supplies neither evidence that Postgres cannot
+handle this query nor a second volunteer able to restore Redis. No production measurements or database access are
+available here, so the performance improvement is unverified. Leaving `LARDER_REDIS_URL` unset preserves the existing
+deployment while those gaps are addressed.
+
+Simultaneous misses can query Postgres independently. Unique searches do not benefit from this cache; check the
+database query plan and indexes if cold searches remain slow.
+
+## Shaped by
+
+- [Keep sessions in the database](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md) and
+  [run background jobs on Postgres](../adr/0002-run-background-jobs-on-postgres.md) explain the existing operating
+  constraints; this disposable cache does not change those stores.
